      <h1 class="page-title max-w-3xl">Hospitality Guest Experience</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-base text-ink/70">A hotel group operating properties across the MEA region needed to unify guest Wi-Fi, room controls and personalisation onto a single connected platform. MEAICON delivered the network infrastructure, IoT integration and guest data security framework.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section reveal">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 lg:px-6">
      <div class="reveal grid-2">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow mb-3">The challenge</p>
          <h2 class="section-title">What the client needed</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose-content">
          <p>A hotel group with properties across the Gulf and North Africa was offering guest Wi-Fi, in-room climate and lighting controls, and a loyalty programme — each running on disconnected systems. Guests had to authenticate separately for Wi-Fi, use a separate app for room controls, and present a loyalty card at check-in. There was no way to recognise a returning guest's preferences automatically across these touchpoints.</p>
          <p>The group wanted a connected guest experience where a single authentication unlocked Wi-Fi, room controls and personalised service. But unifying these systems meant guest data — preferences, behaviour, location within the property — would flow across more systems, raising data protection and privacy concerns under regional regulations.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section-alt reveal">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 lg:px-6">
      <div class="reveal grid-2">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow mb-3">Our approach</p>
          <h2 class="section-title">How we engaged</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose-content">
          <p>MEAICON began with an audit of the guest journey across representative properties — from check-in through Wi-Fi onboarding, room control usage and loyalty programme interaction. We mapped where separate authentications created friction and where guest data was siloed, preventing personalisation.</p>
          <p>The network, IoT and data protection designs were developed in parallel. The network backbone had to support IoT device density across guest rooms; the integration layer had to connect Wi-Fi, room controls and the property management system; and the data framework had to handle guest preferences and behaviour data in compliance with regional privacy regulations.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Guest journey audit and system integration mapping across properties</li>
            <li>Single-authentication guest platform architecture design</li>
            <li>IoT network infrastructure for in-room device density and control</li>
            <li>Guest data protection framework compliant with regional privacy regulations</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section reveal">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4 lg:px-6">
      <div class="reveal grid-2">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow mb-3">The solution</p>
          <h2 class="section-title">What we delivered</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose-content">
          <p>The delivered platform gives guests a single authentication that unlocks Wi-Fi, room controls and personalised service across the property. A returning guest's preferences — room temperature, lighting scenes, dietary notes — are recognised at check-in and applied automatically through the IoT-connected room environment.</p>
          <p>The network infrastructure supporting the platform handles the density of IoT devices across guest rooms — thermostats, lighting controllers, smart sensors — with sufficient bandwidth for simultaneous guest Wi-Fi. Guest data flowing across the platform is protected under a privacy framework that gives guests control over what is stored and shared, in compliance with regional data protection regulations.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

